+## Inputs
+
+This skill runs on the files the agent-skills `/spec` and `/plan` commands
+write. Wherever this skill or its references say:
+
+- **PLAN_FILE** or "the plan": the task list at `tasks/todo.md`. Its
+  `## Task N:` blocks are the tasks. Also read `tasks/plan.md` once for the
+  architecture decisions and risks behind them; it is context, not a task
+  source.
+- **the Spec**: `SPEC.md` at the repo root, `docs/SPEC.md`, or a file under
+  `spec/`. If none exists, stop and tell your human partner to run `/spec`
+  first.
+- **Global Constraints**: `CONSTRAINTS.md` if the repo has one, plus the
+  Boundaries section of the spec. Copy the binding lines from those verbatim.
+
+If `tasks/todo.md` does not exist, stop and tell your human partner to run
+`/plan` first. If `tasks/plan.md` says the tasks live in an external tracker
+(Jira, Linear), stop and ask for them as a markdown task list: the scripts
+read a file.
+
+Run the tasks in the order the task list gives them. A task's
+**Dependencies** line names tasks that must be complete first; if the order
+violates one, that is a plan defect for the pre-flight scan.
+
+## Checkpoints
+
+The task list carries `## Checkpoint:` blocks between groups of tasks. When
+you reach one, run every check it lists and record the results in the ledger
+as `Checkpoint <name>: <result per check>`.
+
+- **Default:** stop there. Report the check results, the tasks completed
+  since the last checkpoint, and every `Ruling:` line added since then. Wait
+  for your human partner to say continue.
+- **`auto`** (the user invoked the skill with `auto` or `all`): do not stop
+  at a checkpoint whose checks pass. Stop only when a check fails and one fix
+  dispatch does not clear it.
+
+A checkpoint is not a task: never dispatch an implementer for one.
+
